---
import GuideLayout from '../../components/GuideLayout.astro';

const title = 'How to Set Up 2FA on Epic Games (Authenticator App)';
const description =
  'Enable authenticator-app 2FA on your Epic Games account, then generate live 6-digit TOTP codes in your browser — no phone app required.';
---

<GuideLayout
  serviceName="Epic Games"
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/guides/epic-games/"
  datePublished="2026-11-18"
  dateModified="2026-11-23"
  lastReviewed="2026-11-23"
  reviewedVia="browser"
  sources={[
    {
      label: 'Epic Games Support — Two-factor authentication (2FA) and how to enable it',
      href: 'https://www.epicgames.com/help/epic-accounts-c5719348850459/account-security-c5719366891291/two-factor-authentication-2fa-and-how-to-enable-it-a5720249664923',
      kind: 'official',
    },
    {
      label: 'Epic Games — Account Security',
      href: 'https://safety.epicgames.com/policies/account-security',
      kind: 'official',
    },
    {
      label: 'RFC 6238 — TOTP: Time-Based One-Time Password Algorithm',
      href: 'https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6238',
      kind: 'independent',
    },
  ]}
  intro="Epic Games supports email, SMS, its own in-app Epic Authenticator, and standard authenticator apps for Fortnite, Rocket League, the Epic Games Store and Unreal Engine accounts. The setup screen decides what it shows you — a QR code, a key, or a number-match prompt — so this guide describes the control to look for in each case."
  minutes={4}
  params={['6 digits', '30 s period', 'SHA-1']}
  ctaTitle="Protect the account, not just the skins"
  ctaBody="An Epic account can hold purchases, linked console identities, and years of progress — and account theft is common in gaming. Save the setup secret, and keep a second 2FA method enrolled, so a lost phone is not a lost account."
  deepDive={{
    heading: "Epic Games specifics",
    blocks: [
      {
        title: 'What 2FA actually gates on Epic',
        body: 'Epic documents where the factor is mandatory: claiming some free games on the Epic Games Store, sending gifts in Fortnite, taking part in Fortnite competitive events, the EOS Developer Portal and the Support-A-Creator program. Enabling it also grants the Boogie Down emote in Fortnite. If a specific feature refuses you, that list — not a forum post — is where the requirement comes from.',
      },
      {
        title: 'One Epic account, many linked platforms',
        body: 'Your Epic account can be linked to PlayStation, Xbox, Nintendo and Steam identities. The second factor protects the Epic login, not those platform accounts — each console network has its own 2FA. If your Fortnite progress matters, enable 2FA on the console account as well so a stolen console login cannot unlink or replace the Epic identity.',
      },
      {
        title: 'A second method is the real insurance',
        body: 'Epic documents no backup-code scheme. What it does document is support for more than one 2FA method on the same account, with one set as primary via the three dots (…) next to it. So the resilient setup is the authenticator app plus a second method you can actually reach — and the setup secret saved in your password manager, which regenerates codes anywhere without waiting on account recovery.',
      },
    ],
  }}
  steps={[
    {
      title: 'Open Password and security',
      body: 'Sign in at epicgames.com/account and open the “Password and security” section of your Epic Games account — Epic’s help article links to it directly.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Start setup for the authenticator app',
      body: 'Under “Two-Factor Authentication”, click “Set up” and choose the authenticator-app option rather than email or SMS.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Take the secret from the setup screen',
      body: 'Epic shows a setup screen for the method you chose. If it offers a QR code, scan it or screenshot it; if it offers a setup key, copy that. Pasting the screenshot into the generator decodes it locally, on your device.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Generate a live code',
      body: 'Paste the key or decoded secret into 2facounter.com and label the entry “Epic Games”. The 6-digit code refreshes every 30 seconds and never leaves your browser.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Confirm the method',
      body: 'Enter the current code where Epic asks for it. Epic marks the method active on the account and sends a confirmation email — that email is how you know it took.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Make the authenticator your primary factor',
      body: 'If you add more than one method, set the app as primary: click the three dots (…) next to it and choose “Make my primary 2FA method”. Store the setup secret in your password manager so you can regenerate codes on any device.',
    },
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: 'Is Epic Games 2FA standard TOTP?',
      a: 'Yes. Epic’s authenticator-app option uses standard TOTP, which is why any compatible app — or this browser generator — produces the same 6-digit code from the same secret. Epic also offers its own Epic Authenticator, which uses a number-match prompt instead of a code; that is a different method, not a different secret.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Do I need 2FA to play Fortnite?',
      a: 'Not to play. Epic requires it to take part in Fortnite competitive events, to send gifts in Fortnite, and to claim some free games on the Epic Games Store; the EOS Developer Portal and the Support-A-Creator program require it too. Enabling it now avoids a scramble when one of those is the reason you need it.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Will 2FA protect my linked PlayStation or Xbox account?',
      a: 'No. It protects the Epic login only. Each console network has its own authentication settings; enable 2FA there separately if you want the whole chain protected.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What if I lose access to my authenticator?',
      a: 'Epic does not document backup codes. If you enrolled a second 2FA method — email, SMS or another app — use that. If you saved the setup secret, paste it into the generator on another device. Without either you are in Epic account recovery, which is slow by design.',
    },
  ]}
/>
